WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.604
A good lesson begins with a book,
a thoughtful question, and someone who

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:06.897
knows the learner.

3
00:00:06.897 --> 00:00:10.777
Bede helps parents and educators
build on that foundation.

4
00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.501
You guide each step.

5
00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:18.472
The homeschooling parent tour begins with a
sample learner, a book, and a

6
00:00:18.472 --> 00:00:18.931
goal.

7
00:00:18.931 --> 00:00:23.065
An Aesop fable offers a
chance to read closely.

8
00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:27.198
Together, you explore the reasons
behind a character’s choices.

9
00:00:27.198 --> 00:00:32.318
For example, Bede asks: Why might the
Lion’s decision to spare the Mouse

10
00:00:32.318 --> 00:00:34.287
matter later in the story?

11
00:00:34.287 --> 00:00:39.800
Give the learner time to think, then
ask which part of the fable supports

12
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.587
their answer.

13
00:00:40.587 --> 00:00:46.101
You can carry the question into everyday
life by discussing how a small act

14
00:00:46.101 --> 00:00:48.070
of kindness might help someone.

15
00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.643
Listen to the learner tell the
story in their own words.

16
00:00:53.643 --> 00:00:58.709
Consider what they understood and
where another question might help.

17
00:00:58.709 --> 00:01:04.789
Then return to the book, a
handwritten response, or a conversation about

18
00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:05.802
everyday life.

19
00:01:05.802 --> 00:01:10.490
The classical educator tour shows a
teacher reviewing a sample learning

20
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:10.916
record.

21
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:14.752
The school pilot uses fictional
records for teacher review.

22
00:01:14.752 --> 00:01:18.161
Consider the evidence alongside
your own classroom observations.

23
00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.394
Review a suggested next step.

24
00:01:20.394 --> 00:01:24.859
You can approve it, revise
it, or set it aside.

25
00:01:24.859 --> 00:01:27.539
Your judgment shapes the next lesson.

26
00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:30.544
Explore either path at your own pace.

27
00:01:30.544 --> 00:01:35.266
See how Bede can support close
reading, clear writing, and thoughtful

28
00:01:35.266 --> 00:01:35.695
discussion.

29
00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:41.705
When you are ready, request an onboarding
session to plan how Bede could fit

30
00:01:41.705 --> 00:01:43.422
your family or school.
